      "text": "The walk down the hill serves as a slow, beautiful transition between her old life and her new one. As she descends, the whistling mountain wind dies down, replaced by the comforting, domestic scents of baking crusty bread and the distant, melodic chime of a church bell calling out the hour. \n\n In a small, cobblestone piazza, she discovers a weathered wooden crate overflowing with sun-ripened, overripe lemons sitting by a turquoise doorway with a sign that simply says 'Prendete' (Take some). \n\n Near a stack of sleeping wine crates, a fluffy calico cat watches her with steady, emerald-green eyes. It looks as though it has lived among these stones for twenty years and knows every golden secret the village has to tell, yet it welcomes her with a slow, knowing blink.", 
